Chapter 13
Cash: why it is held, and how it is forecast
النقد: لماذا يُحتفظ به وكيف يُتنبأ به
Cash is the only asset that earns nothing and the only one whose absence closes a business. Every other decision in working capital is about converting something into it or delaying something that consumes it, and the whole of this chapter is about two questions: how much of it to hold, and how to know in advance when it will run short.
Orontes holds $7,302,100, which is more than two months of its total cash operating payments and nearly three and a half times the balance it held a year earlier. Barada holds an overdraft. Neither position arrived by accident, and both are explained by the reasons and the arithmetic set out here.
Figure F613-01 is your map.
Figure F613-01. Chapter 13 roadmap: three motives, several influences, and the forecast that settles it.
